{{- /*
  Targets excluded from the destination state.

  AGENTS.md sits in this directory as instructions for agents editing the source
  state, but chezmoi sees any file here as a target and was writing ~/AGENTS.md on
  every apply — the repository's own documentation, littered into the home
  directory. Anything added here for humans rather than for the destination needs
  the same treatment; tests/chezmoi-templates.sh requires every managed target to
  be a dotfile, which catches the next one.

  The fish configuration is only written when fish is the selected shell, so a
  zsh workstation does not carry a config for a shell it has not installed.

  .zshrc is deliberately NOT excluded when fish is selected. zsh remains the
  account login shell — see the `command` comment in dot_config/ghostty/config
  and ADR-031 — so its configuration has to keep working. Every activation in it
  is guarded by `command -v` or a readability test, so it degrades cleanly on a
  machine where the zsh plugin formulae were never installed.

  ~/.docker is excluded unless colima is the selected runtime, because everything
  in it depends on formulae only profiles/runtime-colima.Brewfile declares:
  docker-compose and docker-buildx for the two CLI-plugin symlinks, and
  docker-credential-helper for the credsStore in config.json. Ungated, a
  --runtime rancher or orbstack machine got symlinks into
  /opt/homebrew/opt/docker-compose that will never exist — written into
  ~/.docker/cli-plugins, which is exactly where Rancher Desktop and OrbStack put
  their own plugin links, so `docker compose` and `docker buildx` stopped
  resolving on every apply. credsStore was the same shape with a worse symptom:
  `docker login` failing with "executable file not found" instead of writing to
  the Keychain, turning a security control into a login failure. Directory-level
  rather than per-file so a fourth entry cannot be added ungated by accident.
*/ -}}
AGENTS.md
{{ if ne .shell "fish" }}
.config/fish
{{ end }}
{{ if ne .runtime "colima" }}
.docker
{{ end }}
